<title>USA: Duff &amp; Phelps maintains Chrysler debt rating.</title>
<headline>Duff &amp; Phelps maintains Chrysler debt rating.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Thursday it is maintaining its Single A Minus senior debt rating on Chrysler Corp in light of the automaker's announcement it will take an extraordinary after-tax charge of $191 million in the fourth quarter of 1996 for retiring debt.</p>
<p>Chrysler has purchased and retired $550 million principal value, or half of its Auburn Hills Trust Certificates due in 2020.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
